{"id":"resp_85879c8f64582c34","created_at":1795550923,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_9987e26dee4bfbdd","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce a SHACL shape that enforces the requirement: boundary between bottom and lower regions determined by point where shell inclination angle is 7 degrees from horizontal. So we need shape for hullBoundaryPoint that has property shellInclinationAngle with value 7 deg.\n\nWe have termOwners: shellInclinationAngle owned by hullBoundaryPoint. Also property hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint links ship to hullBoundaryPoint. So we need shape targeting hullBoundaryPoint instances (or maybe ship?), but requirement is about boundary point: we need to ensure that for each ship, there is a hullBoundaryPoint linked via hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint, and that that point has shellInclinationAngle quantity value 7 deg.\n\nWe need to use quantityEncoding: numeric predicate and unit predicate. They are qudt:numericValue and qudt:unit. The quantity class is qudt:QuantityValue. The property shellInclinationAngle has range QuantityValue. So need to ensure that the QuantityValue node has numericValue 7 and unit DEG.\n\nWe must not assume targets beyond what's given. The admission says focus_set mode COMPLETE_CLASS_POPULATION_PER_INPUT, owner_class ship. So the SHACL targetClass could be ship? But the constraint is about linking to hullBoundaryPoint.\n\nWe can define two shapes: one for ship with property hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint ; required minCount 1 and shape that the object conforms to another shape (hullBoundaryPoint shape). Then hullBoundaryPoint shape has property shellInclinationAngle with value constraints.\n\nDefine shapes with sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>. Use sh:property for hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint with sh:minCount 1 and sh:node <ShapeHullBoundaryPoint>. Define <ShapeHullBoundaryPoint> with sh:targetClass hullBoundaryPoint? Or just as node shape.\n\nWithin hullBoundaryPoint shape, define property shellInclinationAngle with sh:class qudt:QuantityValue and then nested property constraints: the QuantityValue node must have numericValue = 7 and unit = DEG.\n\nIn SHACL, to constrain literal values, you can use sh:property on the QuantityValue node: but we need a sh:node shape for the quantity value.\n\nSimplify: Use sh:qualifiedValueShape maybe. But we can define a node shape for QuantityValue with constraints on numericValue and unit.\n\nDefine shape <ShellInclinationAngleValueShape> with targetClass qudt:QuantityValue and property numericValue equal 7 (sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal) and unit equal deg IRI.\n\nThen in hullBoundaryPoint shape, property shellInclinationAngle with sh:node <ShellInclinationAngleValueShape> and sh:minCount 1.\n\nNow include source reference as sh:message maybe? Not required.\n\nAll IRIs must be exact.\n\nWe need to include prefixes. Let's craft Turtle.\n\nUse prefixes: sh, rdf, rdfs, xsd, qudt, nltl (the vocab base). Use base? Not necessary.\n\nDefine shapes:\n\n<https://example.org/shapes/ShipShape> a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>; sh:property [ sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint>; sh:minCount 1; sh:node <https://example.org/shapes/HullBoundaryPointShape> ] .\n\n<https://example.org/shapes/HullBoundaryPointShape> a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hullBoundaryPoint>; sh:property [ sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shellInclinationAngle>; sh:minCount 1; sh:node <https://example.org/shapes/ShellInclinationAngleValueShape> ] .\n\n<https://example.org/shapes/ShellInclinationAngleValueShape> a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>; sh:property [ sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue>; sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal; sh:datatype xsd:decimal; ]; sh:property [ sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit>; sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG> ] .\n\nAdd maybe sh:message with requirement text.\n\nAlso ensure reference to source: use sh:deactivated false? No.\n\nWe should include comment as source.\n\nNow embed <BEGIN_SHACL> and <END_SHACL>.\n\nMake sure to import prefixes.\n\nLet's produce final answer.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_991e9930be6fc2de","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix ex: <https://example.org/shapes/> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for ships – requirement I2.2.5 applies to each ship instance\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:ShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:message \"I2.2.5 – each ship must provide a bottom‑region/lower‑region boundary point.\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node ex:HullBoundaryPointShape ;\n        sh:description \"The ship must have at least one hull‑boundary point that marks the bottom/lower‑region boundary.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for the hull‑boundary point that marks the bottom/lower‑region boundary\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:HullBoundaryPointShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:hullBoundaryPoint ;\n    sh:message \"I2.2.5 – the boundary point must specify a shell inclination angle of 7°.\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:shellInclinationAngle ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node ex:ShellInclinationAngleValueShape ;\n        sh:description \"The boundary point must carry a shell inclination angle quantity.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for the QuantityValue representing the shell inclination angle\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\nex:ShellInclinationAngleValueShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue ;\n    sh:message \"I2.2.5 – the shell inclination angle must be exactly 7 degrees.\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:description \"Numeric value of the angle must be 7.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG> ;\n        sh:description \"Unit must be degree (deg).\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":12979,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":12976,"cache_write_tokens":0,"input_tokens_per_turn":[12979],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[12976]},"output_tokens":1588,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":981,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1588],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":14567},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}